  ── 7.2 TRAINING PHASE ANALYSIS ────────────────────────────────────────────

  Phase 1 — Rapid Convergence (Epochs 1–25, LR: 5.0×10⁻⁴ → 4.3×10⁻⁴):
    Total loss drops sharply from 6.2574 → 4.2599 (a 31.9% reduction).
    mAP rises from 0% → 29.66%, AP50 from 0% → 52.42%.
    APS climbs from 3.89% (Ep 5) → 14.95% (Ep 25) — a +11.06 pp gain in
    just 20 epochs, driven by the ASRFR module anchoring sub-pixel features
    early in training before backbone weights fully adapt.
    Key milestone: At Epoch 25 the model already exceeds the APS of standard
    YOLOv8-m (17.40% reached at Epoch 35).

  Phase 2 — Steady Improvement (Epochs 25–60, LR: 4.3×10⁻⁴ → 1.8×10⁻⁴):
    mAP rises from 29.66% → 42.00% (+12.34 pp). Cosine decay progressively
    reduces LR, allowing fine-grained weight adjustment.
    AP50 crosses the UAVDet baseline (64.20%) at Epoch 60 (65.14%).
    APS crosses the UAVDet baseline (24.50%) at Epoch 60 (25.21%).
    Box loss continues falling monotonically: 0.8401 → 0.7901, indicating
    that the Softplus-bounded LTRB regression is stably learning tight offsets
    for micro-objects without gradient collapse.

  Phase 3 — Fine-Tuning Saturation (Epochs 60–100, LR: 1.8×10⁻⁴ → 1.0×10⁻⁵):
    mAP rises from 42.00% → 47.80% (+5.80 pp). Gains decelerate as cosine
    LR approaches minimum, indicating the model is approaching its capacity
    limit on the VisDrone validation set.
    APS rises from 25.21% → 30.23% (+5.02 pp): the Stride-2 head continues
    refining micro-object localization throughout the fine-tuning phase,
    demonstrating that 102,400 high-density anchors benefit from extended
    low-LR training beyond what coarser detectors need.
    Classification loss drops below 0.43 (Epoch 100: 0.4265) — the lowest
    recorded — confirming stable SpatialSSM attention convergence.

